{
  "id": "f16",
  "title": "True and False",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "f16-l1",
      "title": "LOGICAL Variables",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "FORTRAN IV added a type for yes and no: LOGICAL. A logical variable holds .TRUE. or .FALSE., and you can store a comparison in it: EVEN = MOD(N, 2) .EQ. 0.",
        "Logical values combine with .AND., .OR. and .NOT., and a logical variable can be the whole condition of an IF: IF (EVEN) ….",
        "To print them, FORMAT has the L code: L3 prints a T or an F, right-aligned in 3 columns."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "      LOGICAL EVEN, BIG",
          "      DO 10 N = 1, 4",
          "      EVEN = MOD(N, 2) .EQ. 0",
          "      BIG = N .GT. 2",
          "      WRITE (6,20) N, EVEN, BIG, EVEN .AND. BIG",
          "   10 CONTINUE",
          "   20 FORMAT (1X, I2, 3L3)",
          "      STOP",
          "      END"
        ],
        "output": [
          " 1  F  F  F",
          " 2  T  F  F",
          " 3  F  T  F",
          " 4  T  T  T"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "f16-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What can a LOGICAL variable hold?",
          "options": [
            ".TRUE. or .FALSE.",
            "Any number",
            "Text",
            "0 to 255"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Only the two truth values."
        },
        {
          "id": "f16-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this deck print?",
          "code": [
            "      LOGICAL A, B",
            "      A = 5 .GT. 3",
            "      B = 5 .EQ. 3",
            "      WRITE (6,10) A, B",
            "   10 FORMAT (1X, L1, L2)",
            "      END"
          ],
          "options": [
            "T F",
            "F T",
            "T T",
            "F F"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "5 is bigger than 3, but not equal to it."
        },
        {
          "id": "f16-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print a logical value in 2 columns.",
          "code": [
            "   20 FORMAT (1X, ___)"
          ],
          "options": [
            "L2",
            "I2",
            "F2.0",
            "A2"
          ],
          "answer": "L2",
          "explanation": "L is the format code for logical values."
        },
        {
          "id": "f16-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "OK is a LOGICAL variable. Which IF is correct?",
